### Step 3C: Test Chat Authorization
### Tests: Only motard and participant in a conversation can access messages

### ========================================
### SETUP: Variables
@baseUrl = http://localhost:5256
@tourId = 08de221e-495c-495b-8444-af91535a20b0
@motardUserId = 976a094e-da32-49c1-94b3-e59537c63496
@conversationId = 6f73cb1a-a291-4e1a-b90b-f16286fc9873

### ========================================
### PREBOOKING CONVERSATION TESTS
### ========================================

### Test 1A: Ensure logged out (clear any existing session)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/logout

### Test 1B: Try to send prebooking message without authentication (should fail 401)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/chats/prebooking/send
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tourId": "{{tourId}}",
  "motardUserId": "{{motardUserId}}",
  "content": "Anonymous message attempt"
}

### Expected: 401 Unauthorized

### ========================================
### Test 2: Login as participant1 and create a prebooking conversation
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "participant1",
  "password": "pass"
}

### Test 3: Send a prebooking message (as participant1)
# This creates the conversation and saves the conversationId from response
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/chats/prebooking/send
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tourId": "{{tourId}}",
  "motardUserId": "{{motardUserId}}",
  "content": "Hello motard1, I have a question about this tour"
}

### Expected: 201 Created with message details
### Save the conversationId from the response location header

### Test 3B: Get all my prebooking conversations (easier way to get conversationId)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/chats/prebooking/conversations

### Expected: Array with conversationId for each conversation
### Copy the conversationId and update the variable at the top

### ========================================
### Test 4: Get prebooking messages (as participant1, should work)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/chats/prebooking/{{conversationId}}/messages

### Expected: 200 OK with messages array

### ========================================
### Test 5: Logout and try to get messages without authentication (should fail 401)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/logout

###
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/chats/prebooking/{{conversationId}}/messages

### Expected: 401 Unauthorized

### ========================================
### Test 6: Login as participant2 (different user, not in conversation)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "participant2",
  "password": "pass"
}

### Test 7: Try to access participant1's conversation (should fail 403)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/chats/prebooking/{{conversationId}}/messages

### Expected: 403 Forbidden (not a participant in this conversation)

### Test 8: Participant2 CAN create their own conversation with motard1 (this is allowed)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/chats/prebooking/send
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tourId": "{{tourId}}",
  "motardUserId": "{{motardUserId}}",
  "content": "This is participant2 creating their own conversation"
}

### Expected: 201 Created (this is correct behavior - creates a new separate conversation)

### ========================================
### Test 9: Login as motard1 (the assigned motard, should work)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "motard1",
  "password": "pass"
}

### list all prebooking conversations for motard1 (should include the one with participant1)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/chats/prebooking/conversations

### Test 10: Get prebooking messages (as motard1, should work)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/chats/prebooking/{{conversationId}}/messages

### Expected: 200 OK with messages array

### Test 11: Send a reply (as motard1, should work)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/chats/prebooking/send
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tourId": "{{tourId}}",
  "motardUserId": "{{motardUserId}}",
  "content": "Hello participant1, happy to answer your questions!"
}

### Expected: 201 Created

### ========================================
### Test 12: Login as motard2 (different motard, should fail 403)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "motard2",
  "password": "pass"
}

### Test 13: Try to access the conversation (should fail 403)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/chats/prebooking/{{conversationId}}/messages

### Expected: 403 Forbidden (not the motard in this conversation)

### ========================================
### BOOKING CONVERSATION TESTS
### ========================================

### Test 14: Login as participant1 and create a booking first
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "participant1",
  "password": "pass"
}

###
GET  {{baseUrl}}/api/bookings

### Test 15: Create and approve a booking (setup for booking conversation)
# First create booking as participant1
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/bookings/request
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tourId": "08de221e-495c-495b-8444-af91535a20b0",
  "tourMotardId": "08de221e-4962-4817-827e-7c7524ca98ff",
  "costSharingOptIn": true,
  "emergencyContact": "Jane Doe, 555-9999"
}

### Save the bookingId from response

### Test 16: Login as motard1 and approve the booking
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "motard1",
  "password": "pass"
}


###
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/bookings/453d8277-9a41-42db-92f5-123912140da0/approve
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "motardNotes": "Approved for chat testing"
}

### Test 17: Send a booking message (as motard1)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/chats/booking/send
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bookingId": "453d8277-9a41-42db-92f5-123912140da0",
  "content": "Looking forward to the tour!"
}

### Expected: 201 Created
### Save the conversationId from response

### Test 18: Login as participant2 (not in this booking) and try to access
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "participant2",
  "password": "pass"
}

###
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/chats/booking/3001d794-7dd8-4a44-af9e-c563ec6f98d3/messages

### Expected: 403 Forbidden

### Test 19: Login back as participant1 (in the booking) and access messages
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "participant1",
  "password": "pass"
}

###
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/chats/booking/3001d794-7dd8-4a44-af9e-c563ec6f98d3/messages

### Expected: 200 OK with messages
